  },
  "body": "This is an alternative to #812. For cases where an `option` with no `label` attribute is a child of a `datalist`, it relaxes the current requirement that the `option` must be non-empty.\n\nAs documented in #812, there are several reasonable examples of `label`-less empty `option` elements in the spec itself that would basically become broken if we try to add `label` attributes to them. (And my own anecdotal experiences with responding to questions about the option-in-datalist case on StackOverflow and elsewhere is that there are lot of authors/developers with similar cases where needing to label `option` elements in `datalist` would result in undesired behavior.)\n",
